 ```
 
+##### limit
+
+Specifies the maximum number of ranges to take from the header, defaults to no
+limit. Ranges beyond the limit are ignored. Invalid or unsatisfiable ranges do
+not count toward the limit. Must be a positive integer, otherwise a `TypeError`
+is thrown. The limit is applied before `combine`.
+
+<!-- eslint-disable no-undef -->
+
+```js
+parseRange(100, 'bytes=0-1,5-6,10-11', { limit: 2 })
+// => [
+//      { start: 0, end: 1 },
+//      { start: 5, end: 6 }
+//    ]
+```
+
